    <!-- Shown when the "只看有问题的" filter is on and nothing matches. This
         cannot reuse `rules_empty_detail` ("换一个数据源…"), because the filter
         hides entries the user *does* have — the fix is to turn the filter off,
         not to change the data source. The detail line states the counting rule
         on purpose: `UNPROBED` and in-flight addresses are deliberately not
         counted as problems, so a user who sees "no problems" while most
         addresses are unjudged is not being lied to. -->
    <string name="rules_filter_problems_empty">没有判定异常的条目</string>
    <string name="rules_filter_problems_empty_detail">只统计已判定的地址；未判定与进行中的不算异常</string>

    <!-- Data portability: export / import, plus the About entry.

         The export is deliberately a *settings* document, not a backup. It
         excludes the wallpaper image — a multi-megabyte photo the user already
         has in their gallery, and the one thing here that cannot be carried in
         a chat message — and it excludes every piece of runtime state (the
         engine's applied settings, the cache-dirty repair flag, the schema
         version). What is left is a few KB of JSON that can be pasted into any
         chat app, which is the whole point: a backup nobody can move is not a
         backup.

         Import applies each value through the same setter the corresponding
         settings row uses, so a setting cannot be exported without also being
         importable. That property is what keeps the two directions from
         drifting apart. -->
